//! Which functions a **bare** call can reach.
//!
//! Generated by `tools/globals.py` from the Creation Kit's own
//! `Scripts.zip`. Do not edit by hand.
//!
//! A bare `f(...)` is not necessarily a method on `self`. If `f` is
//! declared `global` on a class, the compiler writes
//! `callstatic <class> f`, and emitting `callmethod f self` instead is
//! accepted by the loader and fails at run time, because `self` has no
//! such member.
//!
//! The class operand is interned **lowercase**; the string table keeps
//! the first spelling it saw, so a script whose own name is `CWScript`
//! gets `callstatic CWScript log` and every other file gets
//! `callstatic dunyngolglowattracttrig DirectMotesAt` — measured, both
//! occur in the same corpus for two different callers.

/// `(function lowercase, class lowercase)` for every `global`
/// declaration in the shipped corpus.
///
/// No name appears twice: over 14,301 sources, no function is `global`
/// on more than one class, so the class is a function of the name.
